     "body": "<p>I think we can close this bug. </p>\n\n<p>This is implemented in the code: </p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-import-export-verify/blob/master/verify.py#L190-L200\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-import-export-verify/blob/master/verify.py#L190-L200</a></p>\n\n<p>And here: </p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-import-export-verify/blob/master/verify.py#L222\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-import-export-verify/blob/master/verify.py#L222</a></p>\n\n<p>As well as comparisons: </p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-import-export-verify/blob/master/verify.py#L362-L369\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-import-export-verify/blob/master/verify.py#L362-L369</a></p>\n\n<p>There will always be a sha1, right?  I know there are other algorithms that one can use in Fedora, but I think this is a modeshape one and should just be there (for the time being)?</p>\n\n<p>If that's not the case, then this needs to be more flexible, eventually. </p>",
     "created": "14/Dec/16 10:10 AM",
